[{:adr/blueprint-count-updated-again-8219 "ADR-2607104400's own (is (= 30 (:blueprint m))) assertion updated to (is (= 31 (:blueprint m))), continuing the 'not a fixed invariant' framing ADR-2607100500 established. Added a live-state corroboration assertion ((is (= :blueprint (industry/maturity \"8219\")))) alongside the thirty prior live-state corroboration tests and the synthetic-fixture-based unit test", :adr/registry-field-replacement-8219 "the existing '8219' registry entry had its :repo, :business-id and :optional-technologies fields updated (:optional-technologies gains :optimization, matching job-scheduling/staff-routing optimization needs), and its explicit :maturity :spec override REMOVED so maturity/maturity-of now auto-derive :blueprint from the real :repo presence", :adr/test-status-8219 "kotoba-lang/industry's own full test suite re-run with the local-root technology override before committing -- 7 tests / 184 assertions, all green", :adr/related ["2607104400-cloud-itonami-callcentre-8220-blueprint" "2607104300-cloud-itonami-printsupport-1812-blueprint" "2607100500-cloud-itonami-securityops-8010-blueprint" "2607103500-cloud-itonami-securitysystems-8020-blueprint" "2607103800-cloud-itonami-landscapecare-8130-blueprint" "2607103900-cloud-itonami-buildingcleaning-8121-blueprint" "2607100300-cloud-itonami-missionops-9900-coverage" "cloud-itonami-isic-6511 through 9900 ADR-0001s (106 prior actors)" "langgraph ADR-0001"], :adr/status :accepted, :adr/id "2607104500", :adr/thirtyfirst-spec-authoring-build "THIRTY-FIRST 'author a new blueprint from :spec tier' build, following up on ADR-2607104400's own Alternatives section, which flagged '8219' as a comparable BPO-adjacent candidate", :adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 106, :blueprint 30, :spec 510, :total 646}", :adr/reuse-labor-dispatch-shape-8219 "the registry's own pre-existing :operating-states for '8219' (:intake :register :match :dispatch :follow-up :audit) is IDENTICAL to securityops/8010, securitysystemsops/8020, landscapeops/8130, buildingcleaningops/8121 and callcentreops/8220's own -- this build reuses that shape verbatim, adapted for document-handling/preparation-scope concerns. Now the SIXTH sibling in the fleet reusing this exact shape", :adr/candidate-selection-8219 "'8219' (Photocopying, document preparation and other specialized office support activities) selected: scoped to retail office/business-support services (copy shops, document-typing/preparation services, mailing/business-support services), richly regulated (unauthorized-practice-of-law statutes restrict document preparers from giving legal advice, several US states, e.g. California, require registration as a Legal Document Assistant for fee-based legal-document preparation; copyright/fair-use compliance for photocopying published works; data-privacy obligations for customer documents). Required direct verification against printsupportops/1812 (ADR-2607104300) -- covers pre-press and post-press/bindery SERVICES for the commercial printing industry (industrial equipment serving print shops), a fundamentally different customer base and equipment class from retail copy shops/document-preparation services. grep -rli 'photocopy|document.preparation|office.support' across the fleet returned completely empty. Governor keyword :office-support-governor grep-verified UNIQUE fleet-wide. Legacy placeholder :repo (gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-N8219) confirmed via direct GitHub API 404 check to never have actually existed", :adr/fleet-maturity-after "{:implemented 106, :blueprint 31, :spec 509, :total 646}", :adr/date "2026-07-10", :adr/real-repo-naming-8219 "cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-8219 (public, matching every prior vertical's own visibility), following the SAME cloud-itonami-isic-#### convention as all 136 prior/sibling actors, rather than the legacy N####-prefixed placeholder scheme. business-id updated from 'cloud-itonami-N8219' to 'cloud-itonami-8219' to match", :adr/fresh-governor-no-collision-8219 "this blueprint's own :itonami.blueprint/governor keyword, :office-support-governor, is grep-verified UNIQUE fleet-wide", :adr/explicit-scope-note-8219 "the README's own 'Scope note' section directly names cloud-itonami-isic-1812, quotes its scope (industrial pre-press/bindery services serving print shops), and explains the retail-vs-industrial and customer-base distinctions, matching the discipline established repeatedly this window", :db/id -1, :adr/next-steps-8219 "cloud-itonami-isic-8219 joins the thirty prior fresh-blueprint picks as a thirty-first candidate available for a future :blueprint->:implemented promotion pass. The labor-dispatch shape remains the fleet's most-reused pattern this window at six instances (8010/8020/8130/8121/8220/8219). The underlying :spec-tier pool remains far from exhausted (509 remaining 4-digit-class candidates plus 3-digit-group entries)", :adr/blueprint-only-artifacts-8219 "published README.md, blueprint.edn, docs/business-model.md, docs/operator-guide.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, SECURITY.md, LICENSE (AGPL-3.0-or-later, verbatim) -- SAME artifact set as every prior fresh-blueprint publication this scope. Deliberately NO src/test/deps.edn/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md", :adr/west-registration-deliberately-not-done-8219 "same established precedent as every prior fresh-blueprint build this scope: none of the cloud-itonami-isic-* repos are registered as west projects. cloud-itonami-isic-8219 follows suit -- no :extra-projects/west.yml entry", :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-8219 (community office support services operations) published as a fresh :blueprint"}]